{"agent":"ph-parity","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `[hooks.events]` table only declares `pre_tool` and `post_tool`, but the descriptor’s own `[facts.\"hooks.events\"]` says Vibe has “exactly three events pre_tool, post_tool, post_agent.” If the hook generator emits only the events listed in `[hooks.events]`, a configured Vibe `post_agent` hook will be silently omitted from `.vibe/hooks.toml`; the documented post-agent hook will never run.","digest":"6b4b12e5d00577dc","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/harnesses/vibe.toml:23-25","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/harnesses/vibe.toml:23-25"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The MCP example hardcodes `command = \"uvx\"` with `args = [\"ddflow-mcp\"]`. On a fresh lane where `ddflow-mcp` is not already installed as a uv tool, following this delta causes Vibe to launch the MCP server through `uvx`, which resolves the package from an index and may install/run an ephemeral environment. That is a network/package-install action triggered by ddflow-generated configuration, contrary to the stated conformance requirement of no installs without operator consent and offline conformance, and it can also fail outright in an offline environment.","digest":"3caa87e6fff745d9","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/templates/drivers/deltas/vibe.md:25","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/templates/drivers/deltas/vibe.md:25"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test asserts that the documented Vibe hook event set is exactly `{\"pre_tool\": \"pre_tool\", \"post_tool\": \"post_tool\"}`, but the stated documented facts include a `post_agent` hook as well. If the descriptor records that documented `post_agent` event, `H.hooks.events` will contain a third key and this exact-equality assertion fails. If the descriptor omits `post_agent` to make the test pass, the descriptor is wrong because it drops a documented hook event.","digest":"32192759909492f6","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_harness_vibe.py:18","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_harness_vibe.py:18"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12788,"diff_sha":"91c49547872e2a944f5823bfe5b8fc00ef6e1c2d8d2050cba812eedf5ce8c4c3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/VB-descriptor","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.8,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"89173762c31f5f1f","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/VB-descriptor.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261113T160427Z-ee86d4ff.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"184d8676e3507814bc001826ebf243e20c0f18b1","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/harnesses/vibe.toml":"100644 20a915a162b69edc0aeaf99bd5fe4880735fece0","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py":"100644 e4c4b6472bc748823fec34c7b86355c09eeee191","ddflow/templates/context_harnesses.toml":"100644 cbaf8973fcecc2313591f8a8bcbd1582d3a43e1e","ddflow/templates/drivers/deltas/vibe.md":"100644 b5cbd617856826731281b7d2b2ea49983edf973b","docs/ddflow/adding-a-harness.md":"100644 7f52270033add028e839abbb5501e45ae869b524","tests/test_harness_registry.py":"100644 85f054e0d35467b14720addf10ded4bf7e01c39e","tests/test_harness_vibe.py":"100644 b2b4e07294fbcb0ff078d339fb38ff478fad02cd"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","google"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/harnesses/vibe.toml:23-25","ddflow/templates/drivers/deltas/vibe.md:25","tests/test_harness_vibe.py:18"],"tree_sha":"184d8676e350+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e114724409aebd1e170000166","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":194055,"schema":1,"subject":"VB-descriptor","t